message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "gmira"
abstract: "GMIRA is a library of 21 Claude Code skills for building web interfaces that do not look AI-generated. It treats generic output as decision avoidance rather than a capability gap, and answers it with external assignment: a five block visual direction contract written before any element is placed, with the material world drawn by an external hash index. It wires 7 shadcn component registries (514 components) with a repair and taming pass on every install, holds a GPU performance floor for WebGL and canvas work covering frame budget, DPR caps, shader precision, context loss, teardown, offscreen pause and reduced motion, and gates every build with Playwright across 5 viewports. The name is Syriac gmira, perfect or complete."
